 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 243178,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/cb3a7d0f7c1e20ec.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by HyperPhysics)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>In a clarinet, the mouthpiece is an antinode. This means the clarinet is acoustically a pipe closed at one end.</p>\n<p>The clarinet has a key (the register key) near the mouthpiece. When this this key is pressed, a hole opens at the side. The hole adds a node on the air column.</p>\n<p>Make a claim about the effect of this key.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 762120,
     "content_html": "The air column cannot move down this hole."
    },
    {
     "id": 762121,
     "content_html": "The instrument can no longer play its fundemental note."
    },
    {
     "id": 762119,
     "content_html": "All the notes played by the instrument become higher."
    },
    {
     "id": 762118,
     "content_html": "All the notes played by the instrument become lower."
    }
   ],
